    {
      "sectionId": "section-disclaimer",
      "heading": "Understanding RPGBOT’s Rating System",
      "sourceAnchor": "disclaimer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPGBOT uses a color coding scheme which is simple to understand and easy to read at a glance. This system is designed to help players make informed decisions for their dnd character builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Red"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Bad, useless options, or options which\n\t\tare extremely situational. Nearly never useful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Orange"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": OK options, or useful options\n\t\tthat only apply in rare circumstances. Useful sometimes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Green"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good options. Useful often."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Blue"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic options, often essential\n\t\tto the function of your character. Useful very frequently."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice offered below is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2014 DnD 5e Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/state-of-the-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fey-touched-spells",
      "heading": "Fey Touched 1st-Level Spell Options",
      "sourceAnchor": "fey-touched-spells",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fey-touched-spells-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For a full list of available spell options and spell descriptions, see\n\t"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "DnDBeyond",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/spells?filter-class=0&filter-search=&filter-level=1&filter-school=5&filter-school=6&filter-verbal=&filter-somatic=&filter-material=&filter-concentration=&filter-ritual=&filter-sub-class="
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ".\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fey-touched-spells-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Animal Friendship"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Too situational.\n\t"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Bane"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A decent debuff, but it’s more reliable to buff your own allies with\n\t\tBless."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Beast Bond"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "EEPC / XGtE",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Too situational. Most classes have little reason to invest the resources\n\t\tto make an animal friendly enough to be the subject of Beast Bond."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Bless"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Among the best low-level buffs in the game, Bless remains effective\n\t\tacross the level range even if you cast it as a level 1 spell."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Charm Person"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Given the choice, I would take Skill Expert with Persuasion before I\n\t\tspent a feat to get Charm Person."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Command"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Decent crowd control, and upcasting it works reasonably well. Against\n\t\tenemies which rely on weapons, you can command them to drop what they’re\n\t\tholding then rush over and collect it before they can."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Compelled Duel"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Excellent for tanky spellcasters like artificers, clerics, and\n\t\tbladesinger wizards. This doesn’t force enemies into melee with you, but it\n\t\tforces enemies close enough that they’re easily within your movement\n\t\tspeed."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Comprehend languages"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Take Ritual Caster instead."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Detect Evil and Good"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Too situational."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Detect Magic"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Take Ritual Caster instead."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Detect Poison and Disease"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Take Ritual Caster instead."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Dissonant Whispers"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A good way to break a grapple, to force enemies to move away from you or\n\t\tan ally, or to force enemies to provoke Opportunity Attacks. But it’s not\n\t\tmuch damage so unless you want the crowd control effect skip this."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Gift of Alacrity"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "EGtW",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A good buff at any level, but unless you plan to also cast it on allies\n\t\tyou may do better to with the Alert feat."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Heroism"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A good combat buff, Heroism is perfect on any front-line martial\n\t\tcharacter. The replenishing temporary hit points can mitigate a ton of\n\t\tdamage, significantly reducing your party’s reliance on healing at a very\n\t\tlow spell slot cost."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Hex"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Great on almost any character that relies on multiple attacks to deal\n\t\tdamage. With a Bonus Action casting time it’s easy to cast before spending\n\t\tyour Action to attack. You can also use it to give targets Disadvantage on\n\t\tStrength or Dexterity checks to make them more susceptible to things like\n\t\tGrapple and Shove. On top of that, the 1-hour duration and the ability to\n\t\tmove to a new target means that you get a lot of mileage out of a single\n\t\tspell slot. This is a go-to option for fighters and paladins."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Hunter’s Mark"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Similar to Hex, but the benefits beyond damage are more situational and\n\t\tharder to abuse."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Identify"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Borderline useless."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sleep"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": The 1st-level casting won’t scale, so unless you’re spending spell slots\n\t\tto cast it this is totally useless."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Silvery Barbs"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "SCoC",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Extremely powerful, but also very complicated. See our \n"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "blog post on Silvery Barbs",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd-5es-silvery-barbs/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\nfor details on the numerous abuse cases which the spell allows."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Speak with Animals"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Too situational."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Tasha’s Hideous Laughter"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A good single-target save-or-suck option, but the valid targets are\n\t\tintentionally limited and you don’t get anything for upcasting it."
              }
            ]
          ],
